{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514840-need-some-ideas","id":1514840,"title":"Need some ideas","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-06-13T06:23:52-07:00","id":1514840,"title":"Need some ideas","content":"I'm asking for help, I've been gm-ing few adventures in Chicago year ago and now I have new cotery but one player remained with his character. I have some ideas but I stucked and need fome fresh view to move plot foreward. Plot so far:<br /> <br /> 1. Clan Hecata tried to establish a foothold in Chicago, using Dunsirn family.<br /> 2. Important Dunsirn vampire started to take over some amount of money from big fishes like Ballard -&gt; that was a misdirection<br /> 3. Truly he offered banking services on preffered terms to human power players in the city, and they accepted.<br /> 4. Prince pushed cotery to investigate this.<br /> 5. After investigation ,confrontation with Dunsirn went bad for players.<br /> 6. Players know who Dunsirn is, don't know anything about Hecata.<br /> <br /> Question - how to continue this? Or abandon it completly?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-13T06:44:27-07:00","id":1514842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werewolf43</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514840-need-some-ideas#post1514840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">now I have new cotery but one player remained with his character.</div> </div> </div> </div>What kind of characters are we talking? I mean clan and age wise - or sect for that matter<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werewolf43</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514840-need-some-ideas#post1514840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">6. Players know who Dunsirn is, don't know anything about Hecata.<br /> <br /> Question - how to continue this? Or abandon it completly?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the obvious is, let them learn more about the Hecata <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> And let themselves entangle in the Clan (Sect?) of Death shenanigans...<br /> <br /> But Chicago is full of goodies, so if you want to stay there, you don't have to abandon it<br /> <br /> Critias, the Brujah methuselah who resisted the Beckoning is stil lthere like Helena/&quot;Portia&quot;, while Menele succumbed to the Beckoning and maybe died, maybe not<br /> Critias could continnue his Sire's millenia long war, Helena even could groom Critias to be a next Menele, because after a few thosuand years of enmity, suddenly losing your enemy is terrible, especially if not you killed it... the coterie could be drawn in to this renewed conflict between these two - as a bonus Menele is not a confirmed loss and his returning could cause havoc - again, something the coterie should/could/would solve<br /> <br /> The Cult of Shalim lurked Chicago... maybe they resurfeced? Problem needs to be solved<br /> <br /> The epic War of Chicago in 1993, which saw the city's Cainites and Garou at each other's throats was 20 years ago... anniversaries are alwways loaded with opportunity. Maybe the Garou/Lupin want to celebrate with another attack... the original event has been prophesied by the werewolf known as Gray Raven, in the year of 1925. Maybe the 2023 event been prophesied too? Maybe the coterie managed to get their hands on this information<br /> <br /> <br /> Just to name a few and you can tie these things nicely to your original &quot;ending&quot;, eg. the point where you are now at the moment<br /> \u200b\u200b<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-14T08:52:59-07:00","id":1514961,"title":"","content":"I think it's kind of important to know, in this context, what it means that confronting the Dunsirn &quot;went bad&quot;?<br /> <br /> Like, did they get stonewalled and make it clear that they're &quot;onto them&quot; or did they get beaten into torpor?<br /> <br /> I would be hesitant to simply abandon the thread entirely; if you do go down that route, maybe downsize the intended outcome so it can justifiably be achieved sooner, and have that become a part of your setting. The players probably shouldn't have much chance to interfere, and that might be frustrating, but keeping the consequences from being too bad will help ameliorate that. Can't win 'em all.<br /> <br /> If you don't abandon the thread entirely, then you have options. If they want to pick things up again immediately, do they potentially have more options for mortal targets to investigate that might help them learn more? That could help them to achieve their goals without having to directly confront the Dunsirn Vampire again. Or, if they don't necessarily want to dive right back into this issue, maybe want to give things time to cool off, you can figure out a seemingly-unrelated side-plot that eventually ties back into the Hecata conspiracy.<br /> <br /> If you haven't considered this already, who is &quot;calling the shots&quot; in this scenario? Is the Dunsirn Vampire acting on behalf of the Clan but independently and through their own agenda, or are they following orders from someone higher in the chain of command, who might be setting conditions or influencing the outcome?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-14T10:09:34-07:00","id":1514977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514840-need-some-ideas?p=1514961#post1514961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Is the Dunsirn Vampire acting on behalf of the Clan but independently and through their own agenda, or are they following orders from someone higher in the chain of command, who might be setting conditions or influencing the outcome?</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed<br /> You even could pick up the dangling storyline/potential plotline from Beckett's Jyhad Diary<br /> <br /> As the Rosselini attempt breaking bread with the Warlocks, the Dunsirn Camarilla presence captures their attention. Already embedded, the Scottish family seem a little too at home in the Ivory Tower. The Rosselini are not financial experts, but the Ventrue and Toreador positions appear stronger under Dunsirn stewardship, throwing into doubt their loyalty to the Giovanni.<br /> The Rosselini must act carefully. They could improve their position with the Tremere by outing their cousins\u2019 backers, but this would upset the Venetians. They could alternatively voice their doubts to the Giovanni and potentially rise to the status of major family.<br /> Of course, their assessment of the Dunsirn may be incorrect...<br /> <br /> Not to mention, it is believed that the Dunsirn entered service to the Giovanni with a loophole of leaving the Clan when they desired it. Not interested in Necromancy, the family focuses nearly exclusively on making money.\u200b However, several Anziani now insist that the Dunsirn have to deepen their knowledge of Necromancy in the wake of the Sixth Maelstrom. Being bossed around chafes at the Dunsirn's pride and some worry what this will bode for the relationship between the families.<br /> Tho' you mentioned the Hecata, that part is not really important (but who knows, I don't know the setting you play and what kept and what not) but if you want to take the Dunsirn potentially jumps ship and even petition themselves in to the Camarilla, gathering allies to do so? A Bloodline/minor Clan wih their influence (especially if they made deals and formed ties with the Ventrue, the Toreador, maybe even the Lasombra?) could be a huge boon to the Sect (but the Hecata maybe wouldn't be too happy, the Dunsirn left them... or that was their plan all along, and they are moles?)<br /> Another facet of the Dunsirn is that they are distantly related to Garou (i.e. some of them are Kinfolk), understood to be Fianna (although given their location in Scotland, it could also be one of the old Kin lines of the Black Spiral Dancers). Approximately, one in hundred children has the potential for the First Change and in the rare case that the child becomes a Garou, it is either quickly killed by the family or flees to become a Ronin. Also, more Dunsirn than any other family are adept in Hedge magic, which is tolerated by the main family.<br /> They were recognized at the Family Reunion as a full bloodline of Clan Hecata, and relish the fact that they no longer have to answer to the Giovanni... but they are <i>very rich</i> scottish cannibal bankers, and very opportunistic<br /> Anything could happen","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-14T11:13:22-07:00","id":1514986,"title":"","content":"Thank You both for inspiration cause I found it and I know what to do next. And I found it in Tzimisce topic.<br /> Dunsirn beat them almost to torpor warning not to move against him.<br /> I' m going to run their first meet(cotery) in Dark Ages like game during Batory election in Polish Commonwealth. They will meet Tzimisce and through hospitality and some other thing ( for example Turkish influence on election will favor their choices through Tzimisce intervention), they will own him a favour . And he will meet with them once again this time to repay debt- helping the. Dunsirn against the prince.<br /> Does it have any sense?<br /> I'd like to inspire players to dive in their character pasts. Their old plots, victories and loses. That they were strong together and this is the time to take back the power from current leaders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1784,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","user":"werewolf43","date":". 06-14-2023, 02:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-14T11:27:51-07:00","id":1514987,"title":"","content":"Sounds interesting!<br /> Keep us updated how it went! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-14T22:58:50-07:00","id":1515062,"title":"","content":"Ok, so I have a question, please help me in that. Maby I write nonsense or somthing stupid but please explain it to me. Let's assume that embrace of player characters happened in 12 century.<br /> 1. What generation characters should have then? <br /> 2. Is it possible to remade them as ancilla or less in V5 cause of I don't know long torpor maby?<br /> I'd like to make something sensible and possible in game system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-14T23:13:42-07:00","id":1515064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werewolf43</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514840-need-some-ideas?p=1515062#post1515062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Let's assume that embrace of player characters happened in 12 century.</div> </div> </div> </div>Standarad DA setting then; DA: Revised edition takes place in 1230 CE, approximately thirty years after Vampire: The Dark Ages.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werewolf43</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514840-need-some-ideas?p=1515062#post1515062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. What generation characters should have then?<br /> I'd like to make something sensible and possible in game system.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depending of your game, really<br /> The &quot;default is 12-7 range; the <b>13th Generation </b>is a 2 point Flaw in Dark Ages vampire<br /> But if you play, lets say, The <i>Transylvania Chronicles</i>\u200b-like game that takes the characters in a 800 year long journey? As I said, depending of your chronicle, they could be even 4th Generation vampires, plenty of Antedilivans were around (and they were pretty chill, not ate anybody) or 5-6 generation ones, direct child of a 4th or 5th.<br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werewolf43</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514840-need-some-ideas?p=1515062#post1515062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. Is it possible to remade them as ancilla or less in V5 cause of I don't know long torpor maby?<br /> I'd like to make something sensible and possible in game system.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b\u200b<br /> Yes<br /> You even could be a Child that was bitchslapped by her Sire in the First City in torpor and just now awake... you lived for not even a year, and madea mistake, Sire got angry and you ended up in Torpor and when the guano hit the fanning palm leaves, you became a frogotten corpse in the basement... deluge and ages came and go, yet you slept.<br /> Then someone excavate you in to the modern night<br /> Stalin (in)famously said, \u201cThe death of one man is a tragedy. The death of a million is a statistic.\u201d<br /> Similarly, after a certain point, years only a number that means nothing<br /> This was an extreme example of course<br /> <i><b>Elysium: The Elder Wars</b></i>\u200b from 1994 is the source book you need for an &quot;Elder&quot; game, mostly because it details Elders who are not elders technically, becasue never lived that long, just by the date of their embrace<br /> <br /> So in short, what you wrote is totally feasible<br /> The Dark Ages were harsh to the young (*cough* Anarch revolt happened for a reason for example *cough*) so your vampire could be embraced in the Dark Ages, made a mistake or just Sire got Angre, became victim of machinations or politics, made enemies, or just came the Inquesition, lupines, anything... and ended up in torpor as an Ancilla<br /> Then something awoke her in the modern nights<br /> Excavation, accident, deliberate search party (old friend, sire, etc) or the Beconing itself...<br /> Anything coudl work \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-14T23:15:50-07:00","id":1515065,"title":"","content":"GOD I HATE THE FALGGING SYSTEM!!!!<br /> Okay, clam down... calm down<br /> Lets try again<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werewolf43</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514840-need-some-ideas?p=1515062#post1515062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Let's assume that embrace of player characters happened in 12 century.</div> </div> </div> </div>Standarad DA setting then; DA: Revised edition takes place in 1230 CE, approximately thirty years after Vampire: The Dark Ages.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werewolf43</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514840-need-some-ideas?p=1515062#post1515062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. What generation characters should have then?<br /> I'd like to make something sensible and possible in game system.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depending of your game, really<br /> The &quot;default is 12-7 range; the <b>13th Generation </b>is a 2 point Flaw in Dark Ages vampire<br /> But if you play, lets say, The <i>Transylvania Chronicles</i>\u200b-like game that takes the characters in a 800 year long journey? As I said, depending of your chronicle, they could be even 4th Generation vampires, plenty of Antedilivans were around (and they were pretty chill, not ate anybody) or 5-6 generation ones, direct child of a 4th or 5th.<br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werewolf43</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514840-need-some-ideas?p=1515062#post1515062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. Is it possible to remade them as ancilla or less in V5 cause of I don't know long torpor maby?<br /> I'd like to make something sensible and possible in game system.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b\u200b<br /> Yes<br /> You even could be a Child that was bitchslapped by her Sire in the First City in torpor and just now awake... you lived for not even a year, and madea mistake, Sire got angry and you ended up in Torpor and when the guano hit the fanning palm leaves, you became a frogotten corpse in the basement... deluge and ages came and go, yet you slept.<br /> Then someone excavate you in to the modern night<br /> Stalin (in)famously said, \u201cThe death of one man is a tragedy. The death of a million is a statistic.\u201d<br /> Similarly, after a certain point, years only a number that means nothing<br /> This was an extreme example of course<br /> <i><b>Elysium: The Elder Wars</b></i>\u200b from 1994 is the source book you need for an &quot;Elder&quot; game, mostly because it details Elders who are not elders technically, becasue never lived that long, just by the date of their embrace<br /> <br /> So in short, what you wrote is totally feasible<br /> The Dark Ages were harsh to the young (*cough* Anarch revolt happened for a reason for example *cough*) so your vampire could be embraced in the Dark Ages, made a mistake or just Sire got Angre, became victim of machinations or politics, made enemies, or just came the Inquesition, lupines, anything... and ended up in torpor as an Ancilla<br /> Then something awoke her in the modern nights<br /> Excavation, accident, deliberate search party (old friend, sire, etc) or the Beconing itself...<br /> Anything coudl work \u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-14T23:34:04-07:00","id":1515067,"title":"","content":"Perfect. Thanks for explanation. I always try not to break system framework and cheat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-17T13:08:53-07:00","id":1515409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514840-need-some-ideas?p=1514987#post1514987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds interesting!<br /> Keep us updated how it went! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm setting the stage.<br /> <br /> Year 1177 during fragmentation, when prince Casimir II the Just took control over Cracow from Mieszko III the Old. Players agreed that their characters support Casimir II the Just paving his way to capital. And from this moment the session will start.<br /> <br /> Cracow land is rich with pastures, fertile soil, quarry, iron mines, The city around the Wawel castle and outskirts is filled witch churches (around 10), one monastery, two markets, craftsmen district, inn and few open villages around.<br /> <br /> There's a lot of foreign tutors and merchants from the west (Germany, Italy, Spain). I think that's good place to start.<br /> <br /> Princess is Razkoljna - Tzimisce 6th generation - official character. So I added:<br /> - Sieciech - Brujah 7th generation (a man who was famous in those times, for example he was minting his own coin/ main oponent of players<br /> Siemowit - Torreador - local minstrel, loved by the people.<br /> Father Stefano - Lasombra - priest and scholar from far Italy.<br /> Players -<br /> Ventrue - supporter of Casimir II the Just, doing everything for country and dynasty.<br /> Second Ventrue - his child, loyal, loving money and his position - and Gromisz Gryfita - skilled knight from Pomerania, and his ghoul.<br /> Nosferatu - so called silent men - master of shadows,<br /> <br /> So that's the main court, with castle as elysium. Soon I'll introduce Tremere looking for place to open a chantry.<br /> <br /> Mortals:<br /> Wincenty - first polish chronicler<br /> Gedko - bishop of Cracow<br /> Mieszko III Old - prince and his children: Odon, Stefan, Boles\u0142aw, Mieszko the Young, W\u0142adys\u0142aw III - they will take huge part in plot<br /> Mir\u0119ta - local seamstress - loyal to players, source of gossips<br /> <br /> And Monk named Mi\u0142osz - Warder of Men, Rank 2 Philodox, Homid - future trouble.<br /> <br /> <br /> That's the past.<br /> In parrarel the story will be placed in Chicago. I intend to reintroduce Sieciech in new name as Anarch and main villain. In truth I think that he'll be something much more sinister like Baali. In fact I think that he will be Baali from the beginning. But we shall see.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1784,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","user":"werewolf43","date":". 06-17-2023, 04:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-17T13:40:48-07:00","id":1515410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werewolf43</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514840-need-some-ideas?p=1515409#post1515409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So that's the main court, with castle as elysium. Soon I'll introduce Tremere looking for place to open a chantry.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><b>Chaning the Beast</b> mentions <b>Zara Slatikov </b>who was the member of a now extinct Revenant-family in the service of prince Razkoljna - Zara witnessed the massive turmoils of the War of Princes and came to believe that change was the only constant in the world, attaining the mindset of a metamorphosist without any form-altering powers. For this, she was embraced in 1218 by Razkoljna and tutored in the ancient ways of koldunic sorcery. When her childe had become proficient in the customs of Cainite society, she was sent as an envoy to other Tzimisce domains<br /> <br /> Razkoljna herself was a koldun according this, like her sire, Jedrik who was a 5th generation Tzimisce Koldun - sadly no official information, whos Children Jedrik was, but considering Cracow is relatively close to Prague where Shaagra ruled, whos sire was the mighty Koldun-Prophet, Triglav, the Three-Headed? Razkoljna iss probably from the line of Triglav\u200b<br /> \u200b<br /> So that Tremere will have a hard time openinga Chantry in Cracow <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werewolf43</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514840-need-some-ideas?p=1515409#post1515409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In truth I think that he'll be something much more sinister like Baali. In fact I think that he will be Baali from the beginning. But we shall see.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> Make sense<br /> Zara was and is to this day a staunch enemy of the Baali and their demon-worshipping ways and has studied Kupala and his connection with the Clan for several centuries.<br /> (Tho' she diablerized her sire during the Anarch Revolt\u200b)<br /> The Baali were an ever peresent problem, lurking around the Cathedral of Flesh (witch was somewhere in the Carpathian Mountains so not that close to Cracow... but still)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-17T13:54:35-07:00","id":1515412,"title":"","content":"Thank You.<br /> Any more info about Simon Alaches Tremere regent in Cracow chantry? I am sugested by this oficial npc<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-17T13:58:39-07:00","id":1515414,"title":"","content":"Besides Czech king coronated himself as polish ruler in 1300 in Cracow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-17T14:24:07-07:00","id":1515416,"title":"","content":"The Tremere chantry in Krakow, was th achievement of the 8th generation Tremere Claas Drescher, child of Ardan of Golden Lane<br /> Fulfilling a boon owed to Ardan, the Ventrue Konrad von Aupfholm agreed to \u201cinvite\u201d Claas to Prague and facilitate his insinuation into the Cainite community. This arrangement suited both the Tremere and the Ventrue.<br /> After arrived Krakow, Claas has secretly infiltrated the city in the guise of a clanmate of Konrad von Aupfholm, making his home in the Jewish Quarter, in the cellar of an apothecary\u2019s shop<br /> Claas succeeded eventually in forming a Tremere chantry in Krakow, unknown to Razkoljna<br /> <br /> Simon Alaches is from the 1998 Wiener Blut: Wien bei Nacht (Sourcebook for Vienna, by the game's German publisher Feder &amp; Schwert. Title translates to &quot;Viennese Blood: Vienna by Night&quot;)<br /> It was never translated and I'm not that fluent in german, so sadly can't help with that one\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-18T10:33:40-07:00","id":1515463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werewolf43</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514840-need-some-ideas?p=1515409#post1515409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Players -<br /> Nosferatu - so called silent men - master of shadows,<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking of Krakow, the poor Nosferatu will have hell of a time there...<br /> Gutka, also known as the Salt Queen, is one of the eldest childer of Baba Yaga from Transylvania by Night,and Nights of Prophecy cast a dark shadow there...<br /> She was an old woman - born around 2000BC -, devoted to the old gods, that went out into the woods to meet death.<br /> Instead, she found the hag Baba Yaga, who granted her the Embrace.<br /> Believing herself now an avatar of the Mother Goddess, she went to the pagans of Poland and they worshipped her, granting her sacrifices of blood and salt. When she fell into torpor in the salt mines of what would later become Krak\u00f3w, she lost the ability to feed on the simple vitae of humans, instead needing to feed on vampiric blood. She Embraced various miners and killed them, leaving the corpses preserved within the salt of her lair. Staying within the mines, she turned into a being completely encrusted with salt crystals, with a stooped body, mildewed hair, and frail arms and legs<br /> She was on and off Tropor untill the In the 16th century, when she once again desired death and began to search for Baba Yaga to ask her to kill her.<br /> Her search stayed fruitless and she fell again into torpor.<br /> In 1997, she awakened again and began her search anew, destroying various Kindred communities with her ravenous hunger...<br /> She survived Baba Yaga's demise (IF the Little Grandmother really died...)<br /> This technically Nictuku descendant could be one of - if not the - scariest thing in the night your Nosferatu could immagine.... The faint possiblity of the very hungry Salt Queen is awake would be enough for him to shit bricks (and build a fortess out of them) <br /> You could have tons of fun throwing whispers, stories, even coules to cults dedicated to her who still secretly offer sacrifices of salt and blood to the Monster of the Salt Mines - and consdiering how important export salt was back then, her activity could setback the business and <i>someone </i>*wink wink* have to solve this little problem - not to mention any information about Her and Her Sire could be a HUGE boon to the Nosferatu - or she even could be an ally<br /> 9 out 10 party gleefully sacrifice their Nosferatu member to get on the good side of such an ancient monster (but tend to forget, the Nosferatu <i>never forget</i>...)<br /> Sweet sweet betrayal... or they could &quot;pass this test&quot; so to speak, and such display of loyalty to their friend is heartwarming^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-19T00:18:49-07:00","id":1515518,"title":"","content":"That's interesting. It might me something good to build the atmosphere of sessions.<br /> Quick coterie story. First Ventrue was embraced by <b><a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Hardestadt_the_Elder\" target=\"_blank\">Hardestadt</a> </b>himself, during massive pagan uprising in Greater Poland intended for the role of Ventrue clan will executor on pagan land.<br /> Player character is directly Piotr W\u0142ostowic, a men who swore the king Boles\u0142aw III Wrymouth as his trustee to execute his plans after king's death. Left alone. during uprising he embraced another llayer character without permission and it almost cost his head. Behind uprising stood Verbena mages and soon they clashed, but pc were beaten and repelled. So they turned to third player - Nosferatu embraced after village exile cause of sickness. Nosferatu sneak in Verbena camp and murdered them ending the uprising. This act saved the first player from Ventrue wrath and calmed down the situation. <br /> That's their story.<br /> My intention is clear - cotery disbanded in the future to survuive Inquisition, and second time they will disband during Anarch Revolt. In modern time they are gathering for third time in Chicago, and that is the starting point. <br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}